From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:54:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] media: cedrus: vc1: INTENCOMP, I-frame self-ref, ts=0
 fixes

Three related fixes:
1. Always enable INTENCOMP for interlaced-field IC P-frames
   matching vendor behaviour.
2. Force self-reference for I-frame second fields when ffmpeg
   sends a stale forward_ref_ts.
3. Treat forward_ref_ts=0 / backward_ref_ts=0 as no reference.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Developed-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Piotr Oniszczuk <piotr.oniszczuk@gmail.com>

[Ported to the VC-1 stateless uAPI revision 3 (gus bourg): unchanged.
Items 2 and 3 of the list above are in "increase MV buffer size to
112KB" (in the original series as well); only item 1 is in this diff.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
index 7fffd0410..e89b5d135 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vc1.c
@@ -219,7 +219,7 @@ static int cedrus_vc1_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 	else if (picture->fcm == V4L2_VC1_FCM_FRAME_INTERLACE)
 		flag = !!(picture->flags & V4L2_VC1_PICTURE_LAYER_FLAG_INTCOMP);
 	else if (picture->mvmode == V4L2_VC1_MVMODE_INTENSITY_COMP)
-		flag = picture->intcompfield != V4L2_VC1_INTCOMPFIELD_BOTTOM;
+		flag = true;
 	else
 		flag = false;
 
